---
import Slide from '@decks/templates/Slide.astro';

// The explorations index, live, rising off the bottom edge. Same bleed
// as the Docs slide and for the same reason: a page that runs off the
// bottom reads as a page, where one boxed inside the slide reads as a
// screenshot of one.
//
// This slide replaces five rejection slides. The deck used to spend
// eight slides on eight dead ends, one each, on the argument that a
// number summarising them throws the evidence away. That argument was
// right about the evidence and wrong about the medium: this page IS the
// evidence, all of it, and showing it whole says "thirty-two questions
// and every variation we built" in one move instead of eight.
//
// Three rejections still get slides, because three arguments are worth
// hearing in full rather than pointed at. The rest live here.
//
// What to say over it. It is organised by DECISION rather than by which
// bench a switch happens to live in, every option that got built is
// listed under the question it answers, and the chosen one is marked in
// words rather than by colour. Scroll it. Open one if they ask.
//
// The two questions with no decision marked are honest rather than
// unfinished: the C2 framing question is answered in prose by the round
// underneath it, and the fine-pointer half of read-only is genuinely
// still open.
//
// No dates anywhere on that page, deliberately. When the work happened
// is Matt's to say out loud.
//
// No params (Matt, 2026-09-15). The page runs at its own size with its
// own top padding, which is what it was built to look like. It had been
// zoomed to 1.4 and flushed to the top edge to fill the frame; filling
// the frame is not worth making the page look like something else.
---

<Slide subtitle="What We Explored">
	<iframe
		src="/decks/2026-checklist-component/prototypes/"
		title="Every question the component had to answer, and every option built for it"
		class="live-embed absolute left-1/2 m-0! block h-[930px] w-[1400px] max-h-none! max-w-none! -translate-x-1/2 rounded-t-2xl! border-0"
		style="bottom: -60px;"
	></iframe>
</Slide>
